    {
      "id": "claim_4151866e2e5e44c397e17e08b04aef52",
      "statement": "The Action interface in internal/actions has only a Name() method and no Execute method; running an action requires implementing a scope-specific subtype (KubeAction with RequiredRBAC/UsesPodExec/Execute against the Kubernetes API, or AWSAction with RequiredServices/Execute against the AWS API), and AWSWriteAction additionally fixes Operation() and Resource() so a caller cannot relabel a write as a read or a different operation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/trusted-actions/internal/actions/actions.go#L73-L123",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fef7e92f845d6200a11ad0816f771d69e9e9a260c6f873259a22e9254ae54523:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2c6f4d84f29e4309bfacf2a16508f81d",
      "statement": "New actions are added by implementing the Action interface under internal/actions, self-registering a factory via RegisterActionFactory inside that file's init() (populating the package-level nameToActionFactory map), and adding a mandatory ActionDefinition to catalog.New() in internal/catalog/catalog.go; an action registered via RegisterActionFactory but absent from the catalog is inert because CreateExecution, Describe, and CheckActionAccess all resolve actions through the catalog, not through nameToActionFactory directly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/trusted-actions/ARCHITECTURE.md#L66-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6b14285e6f3240a3930dd447c972d8762ca3a312ce15de7896dedf1719702f13:"
