    {
      "id": "claim_2fed72a257834f70b26c1aa5a603a920",
      "statement": "The rta CLI (internal/rta, invoked via cmd/rta) is an HTTP client for the deployed Trusted Actions server: its Client type issues requests against the server's /api/v0/trusted-actions base path and decodes responses using the same generated internal/openapi types the server itself uses, and it refuses to send a bearer token over plain HTTP unless the target is localhost/loopback and rejects HTTPS-to-HTTP downgrade redirects, preventing silent token leakage from a misconfigured --server value.",
      "evidence": [
